          "heading": "Warner Deans back from injury as Japan host Fiji in centenary match",
          "body": "Japan's Warner Deans is back from injury for Saturday's JRFU 100th Anniversary Match against Fiji, with training camps also seeing the return of props Yota Kamimori and Keijiro Tamesawa and fly-half Shinya Komura. Fiji, now coached by Jake White, have four uncapped players in their squad, three of them in the starting XV: Aporosa Vuniyayawa, Nacani Boginisoko and Peni Naruma. Japan beat Fiji 20-15 in the Pacific Nations Cup final in September, a result that put them into the World Rugby top ten."
